# Siphon.app install

- After every change to the native app, run `bash mac/scripts/build_and_install.sh` and report its final `✓ Siphon <version> (<build>) [Release]` line. A build without that line is incomplete.
- Every normal run bumps `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION`, builds Release, runs the unit tests, installs to `/Applications/Siphon.app`, and runs `mac/scripts/cleanup_stray_siphon_apps.sh`.
- The cleanup removes every other copy: the build product in `mac/DerivedData`, Xcode DerivedData builds, and the retired web-version launchers (bundle id `com.local.url-downloader`: `Siphon.app`, `Downloader.app`, `URL Downloader.app`, including clones such as `WebstormProjects/dl-url`).
- Never leave a copy anywhere but `/Applications`, and never commit a bundle. Use `--no-install` only when the user explicitly asks for a build without installing.
- The web page still runs without a launcher: `node url-download-server.js`, then open http://127.0.0.1:3000.
